# Your applications repository

This repo holds your job applications. The Markdown-to-PDF pipeline lives in a
Docker image (resume-me-agent). All builds run in that container.

For the application workflow (analyzing a posting, gap analysis, optimization,
self-test, build), see `.claude/skills/bewerbung.md`. This file documents the
pipeline internals so edits to templates and individual applications stay safe.

## Layout

```
.
├── user.yaml                       # your personal stammdaten (name, address, …)
├── applications/
│   ├── _template/                  # your generic baseline material
│   └── <company>/                  # one per application
│       ├── bewerbung.tex           # three-line stub, never edit per app
│       ├── meta.yaml               # recipient + posting (source of truth)
│       ├── meta.tex                # GENERATED, in .gitignore
│       ├── anschreiben.md          # cover letter body
│       ├── profil.md               # one-paragraph profile beside the photo
│       ├── experience.md           # experience + teaching + volunteering + education
│       ├── projects.md             # projects / research (DL with GitHub URLs)
│       ├── languages.md            # languages
│       ├── sections.tex            # section order (optional)
│       └── skills.tex              # skills in flex-layout
├── assets/
│   ├── portrait.jpg                # your photo (CV page)
│   └── signatur.png                # your signature scan (cover letter)
├── bewerbung                       # wrapper script (calls container)
└── .claude/skills/bewerbung.md     # skill for Claude Code
```

## Build

```sh
./bewerbung new <company>           # new application from _template/
./bewerbung build <company>         # build PDF
./bewerbung watch <company>         # auto-rebuild on change
./bewerbung clean <company>         # remove build artefacts
./bewerbung shell                   # interactive shell in the container
```

Output per application:
- `<company>/bewerbung.pdf` (complete, both pages)
- `<company>/anschreiben.pdf` (cover letter, page 1)
- `<company>/lebenslauf.pdf` (CV, page 2+)

Update the pipeline:
```sh
docker pull ghcr.io/tobiasbrummer/resume-me-agent:latest
```

## Pipeline conventions

**Who renders what** (critical -- Markdown files must NOT contain what the
LaTeX layer already renders):

| Source | Content | Does NOT go in |
|---|---|---|
| `user.yaml` | name, address, phone, email, github | -- |
| `meta.yaml` → `meta.tex` | recipient, date, subject, language, salutation, closing | personal stammdaten |
| `profil.md` | one paragraph beside the photo | no headings |
| `anschreiben.md` | body text only (between salutation and closing) | no sender, date, subject, salutation, closing, signature |
| `experience.md`, `projects.md`, `languages.md` | CV sections from `##` onward | no H1, no `## Profile`, no reviewer notes |
| `skills.tex` | skills flex-layout | -- |
| `sections.tex` (optional) | CV section order incl. `\clearpage` | -- |

**Markdown renderers** (custom, in `templates/preamble.tex` inside the image):

- `### Role -- Suffix` → `\cvsubsection`, splits at ` -- ` to `Role \hfill Suffix`
- `#### Company, City -- Date` → same logic
- `Title https://URL` as DL-term → title + GitHub icon link
- `: Description` below → body text

**Skills** live in `skills.tex`, NOT in the Markdown files. `document.tex`
loads them at the end via `\IfFileExists{skills.tex}{\subsection{Skills}\inputskills}`.

**Enclosures note** at the bottom-right of the cover letter: optional via
`anlagen: "..."` in `meta.yaml`. Omit for no block.

## TeX pitfalls

- `\dimexpr` / `\glueexpr`: `8*\rem` is WRONG. Right: `8\rem`. `*` only
  between factor and integer constant.
- `\raisebox{shift}{content}` needs TWO arguments.
- `\addtokomafont{element}{}` needs a second argument (empty is fine).
- Cover letter needs `\thispagestyle{empty}`, not `plain.scrheadings`.

## Build caveats

- Corrupt PDF / "Couldn't find trailer dictionary": usually zathura holds the
  PDF open. `./bewerbung clean <company>` and rebuild.
- `File 'meta.tex' not found` on first run: normal, cusdep generates it next pass.
- Markdown cache `_markdown_<jobname>/`: gitignored, delete if behavior is weird.
- Container has no zathura: `./bewerbung watch` rebuilds, the PDF viewer
  runs on the host (point zathura at the mounted PDF).

## Helper macros

| Macro | What |
|---|---|
| `\absenderzeile` | header with name + address + icons (phone/mail/github) |
| `\cvtitle` | language-dependent "Lebenslauf" / "Curriculum Vitae" |
| `\anlagenlabel` | language-dependent "Anlagen" / "Enclosures" |
| `\cvsubsection{...}` | subsubsection with `--`-split (Company\hfill Date) |
| `\cvdlitem{...}` | DL-item with title + optional GitHub URL icon |
| `\iconhref{URL}{content}` | link without underline, in purple |
| `\flexstart` … `\flexitem{}` … `\flexend` | CSS-flex-flow layout |
| `\flexcategory{...}` | skill category heading before a `\flexstart` block |

## Tuning parameters (`templates/preamble.tex` inside the image)

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `\rem` | 0.4 cm | base unit (analogous to CSS rem) |
| `\parskip` | 1.0\rem plus 0.4\rem | paragraph spacing (rubber) |
| `\bildbreite` | 8\rem plus 2\rem | column width for the photo beside the profile |
| `\flxgap` / `\flxrowsep` | 0.6\rem / 0.1\rem | flex item horizontal / vertical spacing |
| `\flxcatabove` / `\flxcatbelow` | -0.4\rem / -0.8\rem | spacing around skill category headings |

Editing these means editing the image -- rebuild via the pipeline repo.

## New application

```sh
./bewerbung new <new-job>
# Edit applications/<new-job>/{meta.yaml, anschreiben.md, profil.md, projects.md, experience.md, languages.md, skills.tex}
./bewerbung build <new-job>
```

Workflow details (posting analysis, optimization for ATS/LLM screening,
self-test) → see `.claude/skills/bewerbung.md`.
